---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Economy" description="Bolivia macro economics, Yungas micro economy, business environment, and why BARK's cooperative structure works.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative h-[45vh] min-h-[380px] flex items-end overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-bark-700 via-bark-800 to-bark-900"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-bark-900/90 via-bark-900/40 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 pb-12 w-full">
      <span class="text-label text-accent">Economic Context</span>
      <h1 class="text-headline text-bark-50 mt-2">Economy</h1>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-bark-200 mt-2 max-w-xl">Macro and micro economic context for building in the Bolivian Yungas.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bolivia Macro Overview -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Bolivia Macro Overview</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        Bolivia is a lower-middle-income country with a resource-dependent economy and
        a strong state role. Understanding the national picture is essential context for
        any project here.
      </p>

      <!-- Key indicators -->
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-px bg-bark-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-12 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">GDP</span>
          <p class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-2">$44&ndash;46B</p>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-xs mt-1">World Bank, recent years</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">GDP Per Capita</span>
          <p class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-2">~$3,700</p>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-xs mt-1">Lower-middle-income</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Currency</span>
          <p class="text-headline text-bark-800 mt-2">BOB</p>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-xs mt-1">Boliviano, ~6.9 per USD (managed peg)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-bark-50 p-8 text-center">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Classification</span>
          <p class="font-display font-bold text-bark-800 text-lg mt-2">Lower-Middle Income</p>
          <p class="text-bark-500 text-xs mt-1">World Bank classification</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Economic model -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <div class="bg-bark-100 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Economic Model</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Bolivia operates a mixed economy with a strong state role and resource nationalism.
            Natural gas, mining (zinc, gold, tin), and agricultural exports (soybeans, quinoa)
            form the backbone. The government plays a direct role in resource extraction
            and redistribution.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            The cooperative sector is constitutionally recognized &mdash; Bolivia's State Political
            Constitution mentions cooperatives in 12 articles and promotes their participation
            in the economy. There are over 15,000 active cooperatives regulated by AFCOOP.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-100 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Key Exports</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3">
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Natural gas</strong> &mdash; historically the largest export revenue source
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Zinc and gold</strong> &mdash; significant mining sector
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Soybeans</strong> &mdash; primary agricultural export
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Quinoa</strong> &mdash; Bolivia is the world's top producer
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-accent/60">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Coffee</strong> &mdash; specialty arabica from the Yungas, growing in value
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 2024 crisis callout -->
      <div class="mt-8 bg-ember/5 rounded-xl p-8 border border-ember/20 reveal" data-delay="400">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ember mb-3">2024 Economic Difficulties</h3>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
          Bolivia experienced significant economic strain in 2024&ndash;2025: severe dollar shortages,
          fuel supply disruptions, and inflation exceeding 20% (up from ~2% in 2022). Foreign
          reserves dropped to approximately $100M, down from $14B a decade earlier (IMF, 2025;
          International Banker). The Boliviano's managed peg came under stress with a 70&ndash;115%
          gap between official and parallel exchange rates. A new pro-reform government (elected
          August 2025) is working with the IDB on a $4.5 billion stabilization package for
          2026&ndash;2028.
          <strong class="text-bark-800">Anyone building here needs to plan for economic volatility.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Photo break -->
  <div class="photo-frame h-48 md:h-64 w-full my-12 reveal" style="border-radius:0;">
    <img src="/images/yungas/market.jpg" alt="Local market in the Yungas region of Bolivia" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" />
  </div>

  <!-- Yungas / Coroico Micro Economy -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Yungas &amp; Coroico Micro Economy</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        The local economy that BARK will integrate with &mdash; smallholder agriculture,
        domestic tourism, and a university pipeline.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">Agriculture</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Smallholder Farming</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            95% of Yungas coffee is grown by smallholders on 1&ndash;8 hectare plots.
            The Yungas produces nearly all of Bolivia's arabica coffee, shade-cultivated
            under forest canopy at 1,200&ndash;2,000m elevation.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Coca (legal, traditional, constitutionally protected)</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Coffee (specialty arabica)</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Cacao (fine-flavor wild Beniano varieties)</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Citrus, bananas, tropical fruit</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">Tourism</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Domestic &amp; Backpacker</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Coroico is a weekend getaway for La Paz residents and a backpacker staple.
            The "Death Road" mountain biking experience draws international tourists year-round.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">La Paz (3h drive) is the primary market</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Eco-lodges and hostels serve tourism</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Afro-Bolivian cultural visits from Coroico</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">IDB $10M tourism development loan active</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">Education</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Carmen Pampa University</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A Catholic University satellite campus 12 km from Coroico with ~700 students
            and ~50 faculty. Cited by a UN committee as "one of the leading examples of
            how best to eradicate poverty."
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Agronomy &mdash; sustainable agriculture</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Ecotourism &mdash; sustainable tourism</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Veterinary Science &mdash; animal production</li>
            <li class="text-bark-500 text-xs pl-4 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.5em] before:w-1 before:h-1 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">Nursing &mdash; public health</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Cost of living + market access -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Cost of Living</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Cost of living in Coroico is approximately <strong class="text-bark-800">$500&ndash;800/month</strong>,
            making it among the cheapest destinations in Latin America. Bolivia as a whole is
            ranked the 2nd cheapest country in the region for expats.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            This low cost base is a strategic advantage for BARK &mdash; it means the community
            can sustain itself at lower revenue thresholds while building out productive capacity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Market Access</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">La Paz (3 hours)</strong> is the primary market for
            Yungas agricultural products. The Mercado Rodriguez &mdash; a 5 km-long daily market &mdash;
            is the main distribution point.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            Existing cooperatives like CENAPROC (founded 1992, organic/fair trade certified,
            Cup of Excellence winner) demonstrate that Yungas agricultural products can reach
            international specialty markets.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Business Environment -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Business Environment</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        What it takes to operate a business entity in Bolivia. The bureaucracy is real,
        but the cooperative structure offers meaningful advantages.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <!-- Tax -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Tax</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Tax Structure</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Corporate tax:</strong> 25% on profits
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">Surtax:</strong> Additional 25% if profits exceed threshold
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">
              <strong class="text-bark-800">VAT:</strong> 13%
            </li>
            <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-bark-300">
              Cooperatives classified as non-profit &mdash; surplus reinvested or distributed per statute
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Bureaucracy -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Regulatory</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Bureaucratic Reality</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Bolivia ranked approximately 150th on the World Bank's Doing Business index
            (now discontinued). Multiple registrations are required. Weak judicial security
            and complex regulations are documented concerns.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Foreigners can own businesses but face a more involved process.
            The 2014 Investment Law guarantees equal treatment for national and foreign firms,
            though public investment takes priority.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Banking -->
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8">
          <span class="text-label text-bark-400 text-[0.6rem]">Finance</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-2 mb-3">Banking Access</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Banking is limited for foreigners. The cooperative structure provides better access
            to the Bolivian financial system than a foreign-owned entity would.
          </p>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">Banco de Desarrollo Productivo (BDP)</strong> &mdash;
            Bolivia's national development bank &mdash; offers loans for agriculture, manufacturing,
            and renewable energy. It is also a Green Climate Fund Direct Access Entity,
            capable of channeling international climate finance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Cooperative law detail -->
      <div class="bg-bark-100 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Cooperative Framework (Ley 356)</h3>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Bolivia's General Law of Cooperatives (Ley 356, 2013) provides the legal framework.
          Key features: non-profit classification, democratic governance (one member, one vote),
          autonomy from government, and regulatory oversight by AFCOOP. Registration requires
          formation documents, organic statutes, and socio-economic study &mdash; submitted within
          90 days of formation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
          The cooperative tradition in Bolivia is rooted in ancestral Andean practices:
          <em>ayni</em> (reciprocity) and <em>ayllu</em> (community production). This is not
          an imported model &mdash; it is indigenous to the culture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Foreign Company Case Studies -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Foreign Organizations Operating in Bolivia</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        Others have navigated Bolivia's business environment successfully. Their approaches
        offer lessons for BARK.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex-1">
              <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">UK NGO &mdash; since ~1980s</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-1 mb-2">Practical Action Bolivia</h3>
              <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Adapted by hiring locally and working through Bolivian partner organizations.
                La Paz office. Reached 29,000 people in 2023. Delivered a 365% productivity boost
                through renewable energy for 4,300 farmers. Focus: regenerative agriculture
                and climate resilience.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex-1">
              <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">German Agency &mdash; since 1962</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-1 mb-2">GIZ Bolivia</h3>
              <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Long-term institutional presence. Programs in water/sanitation (benefiting 2M+ Bolivians),
                resource-saving irrigation (200,000+ rural people), and vocational training.
                Demonstrates that sustained foreign engagement works when aligned with
                local development priorities.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex-1">
              <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">International NGO &mdash; since 1985</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-1 mb-2">Habitat for Humanity Bolivia</h3>
              <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Three offices (Cochabamba, La Paz, Santa Cruz). Housing assistance, WASH programs
                targeting 76,570 people, women's land rights (365 women trained). Active for
                40 years, demonstrating long-term foreign NGO viability.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl p-8 border border-bark-200">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex-1">
              <span class="text-label text-accent text-[0.6rem]">Wildlife Refuge &mdash; since 2003</span>
              <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mt-1 mb-2">La Senda Verde</h3>
              <p class="text-bark-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Foreign-founded wildlife refuge and eco-lodge in Yolosa, 15 minutes from Coroico.
                Rescues 54+ species. Built treehouses from local sustainable cypress.
                Demonstrates that foreign-led eco-tourism ventures can operate successfully
                in the Yungas specifically.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Risks callout -->
      <div class="mt-8 bg-ember/5 rounded-xl p-8 border border-ember/20 reveal" data-delay="300">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ember mb-3">Documented Risks</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">2019 political crisis</strong> affected foreign businesses across Bolivia
          </li>
          <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">Road blockades</strong> (bloqueos) routinely disrupt operations and supply chains
          </li>
          <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">Currency controls</strong> and dollar shortages created difficulties throughout 2024
          </li>
          <li class="text-bark-600 text-sm pl-5 relative before:content-[''] before:absolute before:left-0 before:top-[0.55em] before:w-1.5 before:h-1.5 before:rounded-full before:bg-ember/60">
            <strong class="text-bark-800">No US bilateral investment treaty</strong> since 2012
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BARK Revenue Lines -->
  <section class="py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">BARK Revenue Lines</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        Conservative profit projections for BARK's five processing lines. All figures
        use low-end production volumes, real market pricing, and pessimistic assumptions.
      </p>

      <!-- Summary table -->
      <div class="overflow-x-auto reveal" data-delay="200">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-bark-200">
          <thead class="bg-bark-800">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-display font-semibold text-[0.7rem] tracking-[0.05em] uppercase text-bark-50">Processing Line</th>
