  <!-- Why BARK's Structure Works -->
  <section class="bg-bark-100 py-24 px-6 lg:px-10">
    <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-title text-bark-800 mb-3 reveal">Why BARK's Structure Works</h2>
      <p class="text-bark-500 mb-10 max-w-2xl reveal" data-delay="100">
        BARK is designed as a cooperative, not a foreign-owned corporation. This is a
        strategic choice, not a compromise.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 reveal" data-delay="200">
        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Cultural Alignment</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            Cooperatives are not foreign to Bolivia &mdash; they are indigenous. The Andean <em>ayllu</em>
            system of communal production and the <em>ayni</em> tradition of reciprocity predate
            Spanish colonization. BARK's cooperative structure aligns with deeply held cultural
            values, reducing friction that a corporate entity would face.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Local Integration</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            BARK hires locally, buys locally, and trains locally. This is not corporate social
            responsibility theater &mdash; it is how cooperatives function. Every member has a vote.
            The community is not extracting value; it is producing and sharing it. This model
            has established precedent: CENAPROC has been doing it since 1992.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Government Alignment</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            Bolivia's $325M rural solar electrification program, IDB's $4.5B package, the
            World Bank's $125M rural electricity investment, and tourism development loans
            all create alignment with BARK's objectives. A cooperative that trains solar
            installers and processes local crops is exactly what these programs fund.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-bark-50 rounded-xl border border-bark-200 p-8 border-l-4 border-l-accent">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-bark-800 mb-3">Established Precedent</h3>
          <p class="text-bark-600 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed">
            Small-scale agricultural processing cooperatives exist throughout the Yungas.
            CENAPROC produces award-winning organic coffee. La Senda Verde runs eco-tourism.
            FiBL/UMSA have 15 years of cacao research data. BARK is not inventing a model &mdash;
            it is combining proven elements in a new way.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

